  "worked_solution": "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}4\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{4}(-x+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x{|}_{-3}^{0}+(-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+4x){|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =[4(0)-4(-3)]+[-\\frac{(4)^{2}}{2}+4(4)+\\frac{(0)^{2}}{2}-4(0)] \\\\  & =[0+12]+[-8+16+0-0] \\\\  & =12+8 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
